/S /H6
/P 44 0 R
/T (The Hormuz disruption has made a historically efficient network more expensive and less predictable. Management does not want a list of affected shipments or a ranking of routes. It wants to know: Where does disruption become a business problem, which evidence actually matters, and what should the company change?)
/E (The Hormuz disruption has made a historically efficient network more expensive and less predictable. Management does not want a list of affected shipments or a ranking of routes. It wants to know: Where does disruption become a business problem, which evidence actually matters, and what should the company change?)
