/T (Margin vs. customer relationship : If contracted revenue is fixed, absorbing additional cost protects service and relationships but compresses margin. Attempting to pass through cost may protect economics but can create commercial friction where contracts provide limited flexibility.)
/E (Margin vs. customer relationship : If contracted revenue is fixed, absorbing additional cost protects service and relationships but compresses margin. Attempting to pass through cost may protect economics but can create commercial friction where contracts provide limited flexibility.)
