/P 187 0 R
/T (Service vs. unit economics : A faster mode may protect DIFOT or customer-critical supply, yet produce very poor cost-per-ton economics. The question is not whether the route is expensive; it is whether the premium is justified for the specific customer/product.)
/E (Service vs. unit economics : A faster mode may protect DIFOT or customer-critical supply, yet produce very poor cost-per-ton economics. The question is not whether the route is expensive; it is whether the premium is justified for the specific customer/product.)
